WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.188
Public availability does not mean unrestricted use.

00:00:03.188 --> 00:00:07.010
Information may be visible but still sensitive, misleading outside context,

00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:09.920
protected by terms or law, or harmful when aggregated.

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:13.590
Ethical OSINT begins with a legitimate purpose, appropriate authority,

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:16.110
and a collection scope proportional to the decision.

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:19.720
Consider reasonable privacy expectations and the likely impact on people.

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:21.520
Collect the minimum information needed,

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:24.840
avoid private or intimate details unrelated to the requirement,

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:28.730
and use heightened review before reporting information that could expose, endanger,

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:30.950
or unfairly characterize an individual.

00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:35.020
Consent may be relevant even when a source is public, especially for reuse, publication,

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:36.275
or persistent profiling.

00:00:36.275 --> 00:00:40.800
Organizational policy and legal counsel should guide work involving personal data, minors,

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:44.280
regulated records, cross-border collection, or consequential decisions.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:48.520
OSINT does not authorize bypassing access controls, using stolen credentials,

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.815
impersonating people, entering private groups under false pretenses,

00:00:51.815 --> 00:00:53.680
or exploiting technical weaknesses.

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:57.150
It must not support doxxing, stalking, harassment, unlawful surveillance,

00:00:57.150 --> 00:00:59.000
or evasion of accountable oversight.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:03.360
Proportionality asks whether the expected value justifies the collection and potential

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:03.826
harm.

00:01:03.826 --> 00:01:07.840
A defensive investigation of a documented threat has a different basis from curiosity

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:09.120
about a private person.

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:13.120
Stop when the requirement is satisfied or when risk exceeds authorized need.

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:15.555
Ethical practice includes correction and restraint.

00:01:15.555 --> 00:01:19.290
Report uncertainty, protect sensitive source material, limit distribution,

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:21.310
and remove irrelevant personal details.

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:24.800
When authority or legality is unclear, pause and seek policy, privacy,

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:27.770
or legal review rather than stretching the meaning of public.
